[l_english.STATE_LORE_80]
Aurora knows the past, Alice sees the future, and Bori is omniscient about the present. These three reindeer live in a cabin atop a snowy mountain, and their sole task is to prepare for the annual Hearth’s Festival.
Aside from the festival day itself, which is their day off, they occasionally receive visitors who brave blizzards to reach them. Alice would subtly hint at her prophecies of the future to every visitor, but Bori could only watch as those warnings materialized, leaving Aurora to deal with the aftermath.
Alice’s prophecies weren’t infallible. For instance, a squad of changelings once travelled through blizzards, frostbites, and deaths to Hailberg to consult her about the future. Alice told them that their revered Empress would spend the rest of her life as a statue as white as the snow. Although this seemingly unfulfilled prophecy didn’t invite retaliation, Alice remained puzzled. Even stranger, whenever Alice asked Bori if she had missed any details about the present, Bori’s accounts always contradicted Aurora’s memories...

[l_simp_chinese.STATE_LORE_80]
奥罗拉知晓过去，爱丽丝洞悉未来，而波莉则对当下无所不知。三只驯鹿住在雪山之巅的小木屋中，为一年一度的暖炉节做准备是她们的唯一工作。
除去节日那天都是她们的休息日，时不时她们会接待冒着暴雪前来的访客。爱丽丝曾向着每一位访客隐晦地表达过对未来的预言，但波莉则只能眼看着那些警告变为现实，最终将烂摊子交给奥罗拉打理。
爱丽丝的预言并非不会出现错误，比如曾有一支幻形灵小队顶着暴雪、冻伤与死亡，奉命前来海尔伯格咨询关于未来的消息，爱丽丝告诉他们：他们所敬爱的女皇将在白色的雕像中度过余生。虽然这似乎未能实现的预言并未招致报复，但爱丽丝依然百思不得其解。更奇怪的是，每当爱丽丝向波莉询问自己是不是漏掉了什么当下的细节时，波莉的故事却总与奥罗拉的记忆相冲突......
